## Final Judgement
The fact-check evidence consistently shows that the portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah has been present at Aligarh Muslim University since 1938, long before any involvement by Maskoor Usmani. The university administration, including the spokesperson and vice chancellor, explicitly stated that the portrait was not installed by Usmani but has been a historical fixture in the students' hall. Usmani himself denied installing it, and no photographic, video, or eyewitness evidence supports the claim. The only news outlet that reported the claim (AajTak) was fact-checked and found false. Therefore, the claim that Maskoor Usmani installed Jinnah's portrait at AMU is clearly contradicted by the evidence.

