### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah has been a historical fixture at Aligarh Muslim University’s students’ union hall since 1938, when Jinnah was granted life membership—long before any involvement by Maskoor Usmani. The university administration (spokesperson Shafey Kidwai and Vice Chancellor Tariq Mansoor) explicitly stated that Usmani did not install it, and Usmani himself denied the allegation, calling it a “blatant lie.” No photographic, video, or eyewitness evidence supports the claim, and the only outlet that reported it (AajTak) was found false by fact-checkers. The claim is therefore contradicted by all available evidence. [Source](https://www.thequint.com/news/webqoof/aajtaks-claim-that-maskoor-usmani-hung-jinnah-portrait-at-amu-is-false)